          %p
          #ForSuperLieAlgebras.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebras"} super Lie algebras
                as eg. in
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
              %br/
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
              generality of the above definitions is used notably in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
              where the relevant Lie algebras arise from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+brackets"} Whitehead brackets
              which are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebras"} super Lie algebras
              (see
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "super+Lie+algebra#AsLieAlgebrasInternalToSuperVectorSpaces"} there
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+objects"} Lie algebra objects
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
              to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
              (cf. eg.
              = succeed ";" do
                %a{:href => "#MilnorMoore65"} Milnor &amp; Moore 1965, §5
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#MayPonto12"} May &amp; Ponto 2012, Def. 22.1.3
          %h3#for_algebras
            For
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %p
            In the more general context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} higher algebra
            there is a notion of universal enveloping
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-n+algebra"} E-n algebra
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebra"} L-infinity algebra
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            which generalizes the notion of universal associative algebra envelope of a Lie algebra. See at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+enveloping+E-n+algebra"} universal enveloping E-n algebra
          %h2#existence Existence
          %p
            The existence of the universal enveloping algebra is easy in many concrete symmetric monoidal categories, e.g. the symmetric monoidal category of bounded chain complexes (giving the universal enveloping
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded+algebra"} dg-algebra
            of a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded+Lie+algebra"} dg-Lie algebra
          %p
            First of all if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            admits countable coproducts, form the tensor algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi TL
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TL=\coprod_{n=0}^\infty L^{\otimes n}
            on the object
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
